GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC13): only sprite-sized objects are attached; each polygon knows
its object.

- Patch 0022 attaches the objects that stay put on screen while the camera moves (the player, a
  follower, a mount, a shadow). Dark Cave's darkness, a ring of soft-edged polygons round the
  player as big as the picture, stays put too: drawn in the attached picture it blacked the cave
  out but for the player's sprite (the user's play test). Each object's extent on screen is kept
  as its vertices come (MidTrackVertex), and one wider or taller than AttachMaxSize (72 pixels)
  isn't attached (MidClassify).
- By night the game's black painted shadows (a building's, a sign's, a post's) can be softened
  (SoftenGameShadows: their alpha at most 1 of 31, just visible); the grey blobs under people are faint as
  they are.
- Each polygon keeps its object (Polygon::Object: MidObjects' index, a model or a sprite), and
  the shadow geometry (patch 0028) gives it, so a light's own fixture (a lantern) can be told
  apart from what stands round it.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

